  - tilt above 65° keeps the last heading and says "Hold your phone flat"; compass accuracy below 0 or above 25° says "Move your phone in a figure 8";
  - while walking (on at 1 m/s, off below 0.6) the GPS course replaces the compass;
  - the bearing only updates beyond 2× fix accuracy; inside that it says "{name} is close. Look around.";
  - bad fixes (over 50 m) or dropped fixes keep the last good bearing, marked stale after 10 s;
  - facing locks at 15° and releases at 25°;
  - the check page won't mark a spot until the fix is under 15 m.
